<title>UK: UBS sets warrants on BTPs and US Treasuries.</title>
<headline>UBS sets warrants on BTPs and US Treasuries.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Bank of Switzerland said ithas issued two million call warrants each on the 6.625 percent U.S. Treasury due February 15, 2027 and the 9.50 percent Italian BTP due February 1, 2006.</p>
<p>* * * *</p>
<p>WARRANT    ISSUE PRICE    UPPER BARRIER   LOWER BARRIER</p>
<p>6.625 UST  0.50 CHF	 100-16/32	 87-16/32</p>
<p>9.5 BTP    0.50	     116.75	    105.75</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p>MATURITY DATE   29.AUG.97	 PAYMENT DATE  15.APR.97</p>
<p>NOTES	THE UNDERLYING MUST REMAIN WITHIN THE BARRIERS</p>
<p>FOR THE LIFE OF THE WARRANT FOR WARRANT HOLDER TO RECEIVE</p>
<p>ONE SWISS FRANC. IF THE BARRIERS ARE BROKEN, THE WARRANT</p>
<p>EXPIRES WORTHLESS.</p>
</text>
